A||||4||Hartz||Calling All Turbos - use of turbo timers?||||5||
Z||000000||Hartz||02-20-2001||03:41 PM||||Anybody ever use a turbo timer with their setup?  I'm thinking about adding one to my car.  Any stories for or against?  Installation tips?  Recommendations?  I know I can accomplish the same thing by just letting the car idle a few minutes after stopping, but it gets embarrassing always explaining to people that your super-oh-so-cool-fast-car has to "rest for a few minutes" so that it "doesn't cook itself!"  :-)<P>Thoughts, commentary, or suggestions highly appreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>Hartz<P>'85 SE V6 Turbo<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||N_Man||02-20-2001||05:14 PM||||I remember reading about turbos not to long ago, i think it was in grassroots motorsports.  The article was talking about buying a used turbo car.  They addressed this exact issue and said that at idle you turbo spins about the speed of a cieling fan, and because it really isnt spinning all that fast you dont need to let the car idle down for long at all.  But it also said to expect to rebuild the turbo after about 100,000 or 160,000 (cant remember) miles.<P>Anyways i do believe this advice because we have a turbo volvo since new and never let it idle down.  The turbo had to be rebuilt after about 175,000 km.<BR>Hope it helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||02-20-2001||06:25 PM|||| I have a turbo timer on my car and I definately recommend it. The one I have is made by Blitz, and I got it at Summit racing<BR>  It also reads constant boost and peak boost and vacuum. Installation in my car was easy because they make a harness, but putting one in a Fiero would be harder(the directions are in Japaneese).<BR>Just the look you get when you walk away from a running car is worth it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||billyboy||02-21-2001||01:42 AM||||Dude, buy a Greddy or HKS for $100, it'll save you soooooo much money in the end.  With *any* turbo car, you should let it cool down for at least 10-15 seconds when driving normal, and at least 45-60 seconds when driving hard.  A turbo timer is well worth the money, especially if you're late for work and you don't have the time to dick around with waiting for the turbo to cool down.  Can you tell I've done it before?...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Billyboy<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||02-21-2001||06:15 AM||||I've been driving my GN now for about 11 years and never had a problem with coking due to shutting off the engine after I have been driving.Those timers may be a good idea in theory,but I believe they are unnecessary unless you drive the car hard and want to get out of it right away.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
